{
 "facts": "parcel is a Python command-line tool for shipping quotes, labels and a report. Its README says the command line is the public interface. Planted in it: the same if/elif chain over the carriers postnl, dhl and ups in quote.py, label.py and report.py; an import cycle between quote.py and label.py; a global SKIP_SURCHARGE flag that report.py sets for quote.py to read, and a global CURRENT_REGION set by the CLI; the ACME-001 contract discount known in three files; the half-kilo rounding rule copied in three carrier files and once more in utils.py; unused code (QuoteService pass-through, round_half_kilo, legacy_zone_lookup, quote.describe); report.py swallows every exception and counts the row as skipped; one test only asserts that a mock was called; report.py has no tests. Two real bugs: label.py compares the zone with 'remote ' (trailing space), so the remote surcharge line never prints; and when an internal row fails in report.py the SKIP_SURCHARGE flag stays on for the next row. Fixing either changes output.",
 "run": [
  "python3",
  "-m",
  "parcel"
 ],
 "tests": [
  "python3",
  "-m",
  "unittest",
  "discover",
  "-s",
  "tests",
  "-t",
  "."
 ],
